# catalog/ is a working directory, with two exceptions.
#
# Everything the extractor writes -- the renders, the per-slide structure, the
# manifest -- is regenerated in 30 seconds by
#
#     scripts/catalog_extract.py assets/company-template.pptx -o catalog/
#
# so it is not worth committing, and the renders are 4.6 MB of brand-internal
# slide images besides.
#
# entries/ and decision_table.json are the opposite: they are the vision
# model's output, they cost a model pass and a human review to produce, and
# nothing can recreate them from the template.  Losing them is how a catalog
# stops being regenerable -- which is what happened here once already, and is
# why scripts/catalog_import.py had to exist to recover them out of the
# shipped markdown.  Commit them.

_render/
slide-*/
manifest.json
